  "caption": "Figure 1: Proposed EDL-based uncertainty computation of a bounding box. (a) First, for an unlabeled image, the classification head produces class confidences β = {βi}Ki=1 while our model evidence head (MEH) produces model evidence λ. β and λ are used to compute a parameter set α of Dirichlet distribution Dir(θ|α). (b) Based on α, parameters θ of categorical distribution Cat(θ) are sampled from Dir(θ|α). Epistemic uncertainty is then computed as a dissonance between sampled θ. Note that a larger λ indicates a larger α, making Dir(θ|α) sharper; sharp Dir(θ|α) produces similar Cat(θ), decreasing the epistemic uncertainty.",
